WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.440
The Arrowverse is expanding, again.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.080
In October 2019, The CW announced it had put
into development another Superman-centric

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.140
TV series, this one entitled Superman &amp; Lois.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.680
As reported by Deadline, the series is being
written by Todd Helbing, the executive producer

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.580
of the Arrowverse series The Flash.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.699
Greg Berlanti, who has been instrumental in
shaping the current landscape of the DC Comics

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.000
television world, is on board as executive
producer.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.520
This new series will fill a void being left
behind as the inaugural Arrowverse series,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.180
Arrow, finishes off its final season.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.100
With the other shows in the Arrowverse getting
older, the show will join newer CW series

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.620
such as Black Lightning and Batwoman in carrying
superhero stories forward on the network in

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.680
the years to come.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.070
This all-new story is actually quite familiar.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.801
Superman and Lois Lane have been having adventures
on TV for decades, as far back as 1952 in

00:00:48.801 --> 00:00:49.680
Adventures of Superman.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.870
But while the upcoming series may have a long
legacy behind it, that doesn't mean it won't

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.930
still be trying to carve out something that
feels modern and fresh.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.120
"Blah, blah, blah.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.160
That's a bit much, don't you think?"

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.160
"Honey?"

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.480
"...Yes, dear?"

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.660
Here's what we know so far.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.830
News broke of the show's development in October
2019, and no release date has been announced.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.720
So we don't know exactly when we'll see one
of pop culture's oldest couples back together

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:13.820
on their very own show.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.240
If the development of Batwoman is anything
to go by, the earliest we might see the series

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.500
premiere would be in late 2020, in time for
the holidays.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.070
News that Kate Kane would be getting her own
TV series first emerged in summer 2018; her

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.830
show launched the following fall.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.740
If history is any indicator, Superman &amp; Lois
might be ready to launch by the end of this

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.280
year.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.800
Superman &amp; Lois will be welcoming two familiar
faces from the Arrowverse to its cast.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:42.000
Tyler Hoechlin is returning to don the iconic
Superman cape, while Elizabeth "Bitsie" Tulloch

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.740
is reprising her role as Lois Lane.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:48.080
The pair have established their onscreen chemistry
together with multiple appearances in the

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:52.580
Arrowverse's recent crossover events, "Elseworlds"
and "Crisis on Infinite Earths."

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:56.229
Now, like the Legends of Tomorrow, the Flash,
and Batwoman before them, they're finally

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:58.140
getting a shot to spin off on a show of their
own.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.610
Taking to Instagram to tease his involvement
with Superman &amp; Lois, Hoechlin gushed,

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.700
"I could not be more grateful for the opportunity
to tell this story [...] I couldn't ask for

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.890
a better partner than @BitsieTulloch in all
of this.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.340
[...] Thank you to everyone that said 'yes'
to this project.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:12.740
We won't let you down."

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.820
It's probably a safe bet that other characters
from the Arrowverse may make appearances on

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.150
Superman &amp; Lois.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.110
But while the crossover potential for the
series is sky-high, no plans for how it might

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.569
look were immediately revealed.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:27.100
If all you've seen of Superman lately have
been his appearances in recent movies, you

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.580
might be surprised at the softer side of him
you're likely to see on this show.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:34.120
Supes may be one of the strongest superheroes
around, but when he's off the clock, he's

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.120
also just a nice, sweet guy from Kansas who
likes to take care of people.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.440
The series is said to follow Clark Kent and
Lois Lane as they balance their private lives

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.570
as parents with their professional lives as
journalists — as well as Clark's crime-fighting

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:49.140
career while moonlighting as the Man of Steel,
obviously.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:54.340
Though no specific plot for Superman &amp; Lois
has been confirmed by the CW, it'll likely

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:59.239
feel somewhat similar to the '90s reincarnation
of the couple in Lois &amp; Clark: The New Adventures

00:02:59.240 --> 00:02:59.920
of Superman.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.720
That series focused more on the couple's relationship
than Superman's crime-fighting, and we imagine

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.200
that dynamic will be similar here.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:09.860
Only this time, there will be the pitter-patter
of baby feet to contend with as well.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.840
While she couldn't reveal much else about
the show's plot, Tulloch did speak briefly

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:18.680
to TVGuide about Superman &amp; Lois, teasing
that the story is something quite special:

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.240
The actress said,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.599
"When Todd Helbing was telling me about the
story for the pilot script for Superman &amp; Lois

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:24.709
I got chills.

00:03:24.709 --> 00:03:28.599
It's so good, and it's something we haven't
seen before with them, so I think it's going

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.500
to be great."

